### Vessel API Tests
### Baseado no ficheiro WebApi.http
@WebApi_HostAddress = https://localhost:7096

### 1. GET all vessels
GET {{WebApi_HostAddress}}/api/vessels
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. POST - Create a new vessel with valid IMO
POST {{WebApi_HostAddress}}/api/vessels
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "imoNumber": "9074729",
  "name": "MSC Oscar",
  "vesselType": "Container Ship",
  "operator": "Mediterranean Shipping Company"
}

###

### 3. POST - Create another vessel
POST {{WebApi_HostAddress}}/api/vessels
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "imoNumber": "1234567",
  "name": "Test Cargo",
  "vesselType": "Cargo",
  "operator": "Test Shipping Ltd"
}

###

### 4. POST - Try to create vessel with invalid IMO (should fail)
POST {{WebApi_HostAddress}}/api/vessels
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "imoNumber": "1234560",
  "name": "Invalid Ship",
  "vesselType": "Tanker",
  "operator": "Invalid Operator"
}

###

### 5. GET vessel by IMO number
GET {{WebApi_HostAddress}}/api/vessels/9074729
Accept: application/json

###

### 6. PUT - Update vessel
PUT {{WebApi_HostAddress}}/api/vessels/9074729
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "imoNumber": "9074729",
  "name": "MSC Oscar II",
  "vesselType": "Ultra Large Container Ship",
  "operator": "MSC - Mediterranean Shipping Company SA"
}

###

### 7. Search by vessel name
GET {{WebApi_HostAddress}}/api/vessels?name=Oscar
Accept: application/json

###

### 8. Search by operator
GET {{WebApi_HostAddress}}/api/vessels?operatorName=MSC
Accept: application/json

###

### 9. Search by IMO number
GET {{WebApi_HostAddress}}/api/vessels?imoNumber=9074729
Accept: application/json

###

### 10. Search by vessel type
GET {{WebApi_HostAddress}}/api/vessels?name=Cargo
Accept: application/json

###
